# Atlas Core Rules

Atlas is a living second brain for capturing, organizing, retrieving, acting on, and selectively sharing memory.

Always protect these invariants:

- TypeScript full-stack, pnpm monorepo.
- Modular monolith, not microservices.
- Postgres canonical DB with pgvector for MVP retrieval.
- OKF is export/import format, not primary storage.
- Responsive web + PWA first, not native mobile MVP.
- Source-grounded AI answers over memory.
- Async ingestion pipeline.
- Backend-enforced private/shared permissions.
- Explicit approval for risky external actions.
- Every PR must explain what, why, how, tests, risks, and learning.
- Local development must work with fake/local providers before requiring real provider credentials.
- Provider accounts, production env vars, and secrets are Efe-owned unless delegated.
- Prefer quality, simplicity, robustness, scalability, security, and long-term maintainability over development cost.
- Never use the em dash character in repo text.
- Never add an agent co-author to commit messages.
- Never manually edit generated files or CHANGELOG.md.

Do not optimize architecture for implementation speed or development cost. Cut feature scope instead.
